# TLS termination for one AgentBox tenant. Reference material only: nothing in
# this repository installs or manages a proxy.
#
# The rendered tenant .env pins OPENCLAW_PUBLISH_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1, so the
# Gateway listens only on loopback and this proxy is the sole way in.
#
# TLS is required even for a token-mode operator box: the renderer sets
# gateway.controlUi.allowedOrigins to spec.publicOrigin, so reaching the Gateway
# by IP is refused, and the Control UI WebSocket must be wss://.

# Replace with spec.publicOrigin from the tenant manifest.
agentbox.example.ch {
	encode zstd gzip

	# Replace 18789 with spec.gatewayPort. reverse_proxy upgrades WebSocket
	# connections on its own, which the Control UI needs.
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:18789
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Employee tenants: identity-aware proxy
#
# The block above is enough for token mode, where the only user is an AlpenData
# operator holding the Gateway token. It is NOT enough for employees.
#
# An employee tenant needs an identity-aware proxy in front, and that proxy is
# part of the security boundary. It must:
#
#   1. authenticate the employee against the customer's identity provider;
#   2. OVERWRITE, never forward, the configured user header;
#   3. OVERWRITE x-openclaw-scopes from a server-side group mapping
#        employee: operator.read,operator.write
#        admin:    operator.read,operator.write,operator.admin
#   4. connect from an address listed in gateway.trustedProxies;
#   5. leave no path that reaches the Gateway without passing through it.
#
# A scope value copied from the browser is an authorization bypass. Caddy alone
# does not authenticate users; pair it with an OIDC forward-auth service, or use
# a proxy that speaks OIDC natively.
#
# Trusted-proxy mode also rejects a request whose source is loopback unless
# gateway.auth.trustedProxy.allowLoopback is set. A proxy in a container on the
# same host arrives from the Docker bridge and is treated as remote, which is
# what you want. See docs/gateway/trusted-proxy-auth.md before shipping this.
